-- title:
--   Valuation ring of a complete rank-one field is an adic frame
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative domain, $\pi \in \mathcal O$ irreducible, and assume $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {π}) 𝒪`, i.e. precomplete and Hausdorff for the $(\pi)$-adic filtration). Let $K_0$ be a field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$, and let $C$ be a field extension of $K_0$ carrying a valuation $v$ with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$, complete for the induced topology, and of rank one in the following elementwise sense: for all $x, y \in C$ with $v(x) < 1$ and $y \neq 0$ there is $n \in \mathbb N$ with $v(x)^n \le v(y)$. Assume the elements of $K_0$ of valuation at most $1$ in $C$ are exactly those coming from $\mathcal O$: $x \in \operatorname{range}(\mathcal O \to K_0)$ iff $v(x) \le 1$ in $C$. Let $\varpi$ be a pseudo-uniformiser of $K_0$ relative to $C$, that is an element $\varpi.\varpi \in K_0$ with $0 < v(\varpi.\varpi) < 1$ in $C$ and such that for every $a \in K_0^{\times}$ some $N$ satisfies $v(\varpi.\varpi)^N \le v(a) \le v(\varpi.\varpi)^{-N}$, and suppose $\pi$ maps to $\varpi.\varpi$ in $K_0$. Finally let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a subalgebra-candidate of $C$ via an algebra map $R \to C$, with $\mathcal O \to R \to C$ and $\mathcal O \to K_0 \to C$ compatible, such that $R \to C$ is injective and its image is precisely the valuation ring: $v(c) \le 1$ iff $c \in \operatorname{range}(R \to C)$. Then $(\pi, \varpi, R)$ is an adic frame, i.e. `IsAdicFrame π ϖ R` holds: $\pi$ is irreducible, $R \to C$ is injective with image $\{v \le 1\}$, $R$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete and Hausdorff for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ in $R$, the elements of $K_0$ with $v \le 1$ in $C$ are exactly those from $\mathcal O$, the image of $K_0$ in $C$ is closed, and $\pi$ and $\varpi.\varpi$ have the same image in $C$.
--
--   This is the recognition criterion which turns a complete rank-one valued field $C$ over the fraction field of a complete discrete valuation ring, together with a ring realising its valuation ring, into the base data (an adic frame) on which the formal upper half-plane and its Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation are built. The two assertions beyond the hypotheses are the $(\pi)$-adic completeness and separatedness of the valuation ring and the closedness of $K_0$ in $C$. It is used in the construction of the function field of a Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient.
